### updateTexImage()

Source: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/SurfaceTexture

Updates the texture image to the most recent frame from the image stream. This must be called while the owning OpenGL ES context is current on the calling thread and implicitly binds its texture to the `GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES` texture target.

```APIDOC
## updateTexImage()

### Description
Updates the texture image to the most recent frame from the image stream. This may only be called while the OpenGL ES context that owns the texture is current on the calling thread. It will implicitly bind its texture to the `GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES` texture target.

### Method
`public void updateTexImage ()`

### Endpoint
N/A (Method within a class)

### Parameters
None

### Request Example
N/A

